  "requestTimestamp": "2026-07-19T01:39:39.940Z",
  "answer": "### Short Answer\nThe deadline for filing the annual income tax return of an individual is on or before the fifteenth (15th) day of April of each year, covering income for the preceding taxable year.\n\n### Controlling Authorities\nThis is established under Section 51(C)(1) of the National Internal Revenue Code (NIRC).\n\n### Interpretation\nSection 51(C)(1) of the NIRC explicitly states that individuals must file their income tax returns by April 15 of each year for the income earned in the previous year. This deadline applies to all individual taxpayers, including citizens and resident aliens.\n\n### Practical Meaning\nTaxpayers should ensure that their income tax returns are prepared and submitted by the April 15 deadline to avoid penalties and interest for late filing. It is advisable to keep track of income and deductions throughout the year to facilitate timely and accurate filing.",
